module fluorescence

// NOTE: this paper is an ontology paper (EXACT2), not itself a full step-by-step wet-lab
// protocol. The only fully parameterized, concrete example it gives is the worked
// "Adjust to 10% TCA. Incubate at 30C overnight." fragment (Figures 2-3), where the paper
// itself walks through disambiguating 'TCA' -> Trichloroacetic acid and 'overnight' -> 16
// hours. That fragment is translated below. The paper's other example (the Physarum
// polycephalum streak/transfer Petri net fragment, Figure 4) is NOT modeled: the paper
// explicitly states this workflow is incomplete as formalized (it lacks a 'time point'
// descriptor and gives no concrete temperature/duration values), so there is nothing
// executable to translate from it.
//
// EXACT2's <adjust> experimental action has no BioScript equivalent, so it is mapped to
// 'mix' (combining the sample with the TCA solution), the nearest available primitive.
// The biochemical entity being incubated is left unspecified in the paper's own example --
// Figure 3's output explicitly records "Biochemical entity: not found" -- and is modeled
// generically as 'sample'. The ambiguous 'overnight' duration is resolved to the paper's own
// disambiguated default value of 16 hours (960 minutes), per its Figure 3 worked output.

manifest sample
manifest tca_solution

instructions:

// "Adjust to 10% TCA" -- combine the sample with 10% Trichloroacetic acid solution
s = dispense sample
tca = dispense 10 units of tca_solution
adjusted = mix s with tca

// "Incubate at 30C overnight" -- disambiguated by EXACT2's own worked example to 30 C, 16 h
heat adjusted at 30c for 960m

dispose adjusted
